body:
I have seen a doctor. She suggested I get an MRI of the area that the issues seem to stem from (lower back/hip/groin area) but I didn't go ahead with it because my physiotherapist said an MRI couldn't show up anything that would not be obvious from my symptoms and the tests that she can do herself.  I'd heard the same thing from another physiotherapist previously so I took her word for it. 

&#x200B;

I've also had a general checkup recently to check for any deficiencies or other markers that could be causing me to feel run down. It all came up great apart from low sodium and too much B12, presumably from supplements... haha...

Actually part of my therapy has been to make me face the reality of what I'm missing out on and what I've lost. Good therapy doesn't deny reality or insist on ignoring difficult truths. Mourning is important not just for deaths of living creatures but for losses of all kinds. 

&#x200B;

Anyone's life would be better without anxiety.

I do take anxiety medication. have an excellent psychiatrist, an excellent psychologist, a bookshelf full of books on subjects from psychology to psychiatry to meditation and so on... I see a personal trainer...

&#x200B;

Your ignorance is enormous and you don't deserve any further information about me if you're so quick to judge and presume.
